WEBVTT

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:05.000
When was the last time you owned your values

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.880
and those values were the reason for a great day at work

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.600
or a draining one?

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.080
Your first move is to get crystal clear

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.800
on your own leadership blueprint.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.040
We call this your M.V.P. plus V,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.000
your mission, vision, purpose, and values.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.360
This is what we call your foundation for forever,

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.200
for your entire life.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.200
And it directly informs how you lead.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.760
Let's quickly define the terms so you can have clarity

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.560
as you go through your playbook drill.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:45.640
Your purpose is your fundamental why.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.320
It's the lasting impact you want to have.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.960
Your vision is your where.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.560
It's the vivid picture of the future

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.320
and what you're creating,

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.940
both personally and professionally.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.460
And your mission is your how.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.360
It's what you do every day to make that vision a reality.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.300
When you lead from this place of clarity,

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.700
your coaching is an act of alignment.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.580
When you're disconnected from it,

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:18.760
you risk misalignment, which can lead to burnout.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:21.800
That internal conflict between what you value

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:25.240
and what you do is massively energy draining.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.440
I once coached an executive who was brilliant,

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.120
but miserable.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.400
After this exercise,

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.120
she realized a core value was creativity,

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.680
yet her role had become purely administrative.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:43.120
Her work was misaligned with her purpose.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.800
Armed with this clarity,

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:49.320
she proposed carving out time for an innovation task force.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.640
Her leader agreed,

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.640
and her energy and performance skyrocketed

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.360
because her work was now fueling her.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:01.200
Now, head to your playbook for drill 2.2.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.120
Your play is to complete the M.V.P. audit

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:07.260
to define your own mission, vision, and purpose.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.660
Then identify one low value task you can delegate

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:15.720
or diminish this week to better align your M.V.P.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.160
and reclaim your energy.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.160
Once you've completed that drill,

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.980
join me in the next video,

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:25.260
where we'll shift focus from leading self

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:28.300
to leading others by creating a climate

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.120
of psychological safety.
